{
	"_comment": "Speeds keep a 30:20:18:35:22 ratio, scaled so a Scooter 20 sails Rome-Tunis in about 60 s. range_nm is the longest single leg the model can sail (Scooter 20: 1 min 30 s of sailing, Feeder 100: 2 min 40 s since it was sped up to 4.82 nm/s, Feedermax 200: 6 min, Trans Atlantic: Rome to New York, Dominator: 9,000 nm). max_owned is how many of each model the player can own. map_size (length, width in pixels) and map_color are how the ship is drawn on the map: container ships run yellow to red and gas tankers light green to dark blue (smallest to biggest), recovery boats brown (darker = bigger), icebreakers icebreaker red, tugs black. breakdown_factor scales the chance of a random breakdown (bigger ships are sturdier). fuel_tank is in fuel units; fuel_per_s is burned every second at sea, whatever the speed. Burn was set so fuel cost about a third of a leg's pay at full speed (about 40% since the fuel price rose 20%), and tanks are sized so a ship leaving at 100% maintenance can just finish a range_nm leg (plus 1 s spare) while wearing and slowing on the way. Icebreakers (icebreaker: diesel or nuclear) sail no routes either: they are stationed at an ice area and lead convoys through its seasonal ice (game_config icebreaking); they pay their own fuel and repairs. Recovery boats (recovery: true) sail no routes: they recover lost ships, and range_nm is the longest recovery job they can do. carries lists the models a recovery boat can carry (none listed = any). Tugs (tug: true) sail no routes either: they are based two to a port on your routes and push or drag lost ships within reach_nm of their port back in (game_config tugs); range_nm is how far one can sail to move to another port. The Mammoth costs the most to run; the Buffalo, the size of a Trans Atlantic, carries only Scooter 20s, Feeder 100s, Feedermax 200s and Coastal tankers and costs about a tenth as much to run. wear_pct_per_min is maintenance lost per minute of running at sea (the Dominator and Mammoth wear at half rate; speed is top speed x maintenance, so a ship at 0% stops); repair_cost_per_pct is set so repairs cost about 10% of what the ship earns sailing. dock_s is how long a ship unloads and loads at each port; repair, then refuel, each take refill_phase_s of that time. category groups the models in the shop: container ships, gas tankers and recovery boats. capacity is in the unit of the model's cargo (containers, tons, head, vehicles); cargo lists the commodities it can carry (data/markets.json). Each tanker size is 10x the cargo and 15% slower than the last. The new lines' fuel, tank and repair numbers follow the same rules as the old ones (fuel about 40% and repairs 10% of what a similar ship earned under the old flat pay, before both were halved). unlock_level is the company level needed to buy the model. seaway: true if the model fits the St. Lawrence Seaway and can sail to Great Lakes ports (Scooter 20, Feeder 100, Feedermax 200, Laker, Grain Laker, Cattle Coaster, Livestock Carrier, Coastal and Car Hopper, and both recovery boats so lake ships can be rescued). slot_every overrides game_config ship_slots' [start, every] every value for one model (the Scooter 20 and Feeder 100 get a slot every 2 levels). first_price, if set, is what the company pays for its first ever ship of that model (the Buffalo's first is $150,000); later ones cost price, and a ship sells for half what was paid for it. xp_first_level is the ship XP a ship needs for its first level; each level after costs 5% more (game_config ship_level_growth). Bigger models need disproportionately more, so small ships level fastest. min_port is the smallest port band the model can dock at (game_config port_sizes): tier-4 ships (Trans Atlantic and the other lines' middle ships) need Medium, tier-5 ships (Dominator and the other lines' biggest) need Large; smaller ships and recovery boats dock anywhere. Recovery boats earn XP by the mile on recovery jobs (game_config recovery_xp): a Buffalo job averages about 1,050 nm and a Mammoth one about 2,700 nm, so the first level takes about one job and level 30 about 20 hours of play. tier (1 to 5, from the smallest of a line to the biggest; service ships by their size) sets the captains and crew a model needs (game_config crew).",
